<id/18/1828/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Cantharides"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the commercial name for various blistering beetles, often termed Spanish flies; but which are also imported from China, Russia, Sicily, and Germany. The large genus *Mylabris* furnishes many insects possessing strong vesicatory powers. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 79]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals): Named materia medica (castoreum, ginseng, cubebs, scammony, maidenhair, liquorice juice, quassia, cocculus indicus, serpentary, asafoetida, cantharides, hellebore, pipsissewa, ipecacuanha) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 4 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×4. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×4. Top routes: Holland → United Kingdom ×1; Italy → United Kingdom ×1; World → United Kingdom ×1; Germany → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1828" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cantharides"@en ;
